Build type: makefile (plain GNU Make, no ./configure)
Source: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/releases/download/v1.4.4/zstd-1.4.4.tar.gz
        file_size=1948426 file_md5=487f7ee1562dee7c1c8adf85e2a63df9
Build order: foundation, before Mesa 25.3.6 (mesa-core/Mesa). No other package
in this repo declares it.
No upstream GoboLinux recipe exists for Zstd (checked the gobolinux/Recipes
tree: no Zstd/ELFUtils-style entry), so this recipe was written for this repo
from the tag tarball. The version is the ISO's own 1.4.4 -- the recipe exists to
put libzstd.pc in the dependency graph, not to upgrade it.
Mesa side: meson.options has 'zstd' as a feature (auto). meson.build then does
dependency('libzstd') and defines HAVE_ZSTD, used by the gallium shader cache
for compressed entries. Because the feature is auto, a missing recipe/libtool
did not break the build before -- it just left the dependency undocumented.
Build: `make` with no explicit target runs Makefile's default rule
       `default: lib-release zstd-release`, i.e. the shared+static library
       (lib/Makefile) and the zstd CLI (programs/Makefile). The heavy
       `all: allmost examples manual contrib` target is deliberately NOT used
       (it needs asciidoctor and builds the contrib dictionaries/packages).
Install: `make install` -> `make -C lib install` (install-pc, install-static,
       install-shared, install-includes) and `make -C programs install`
       (zstd + zstdcat/unzstd/zstdmt symlinks, zstdless/zstdgrep, man pages).
PREFIX is the only variable needed: lib/Makefile computes
LIBDIR=$(exec_prefix)/lib, INCLUDEDIR=$(PREFIX)/include,
PKGCONFIGDIR=$(LIBDIR)/pkgconfig and programs/Makefile computes
BINDIR=$(exec_prefix)/bin, so PREFIX=$target reproduces the installed layout
exactly:
  bin/{zstd,zstdcat,zstdgrep,zstdless,zstdmt,unzstd}
  lib/libzstd.so.1.x.y + libzstd.so.1 + libzstd.so + libzstd.a
  lib/pkgconfig/libzstd.pc
  include/{zstd.h,zstd_errors.h,zbuff.h,zdict.h}
  share/man/man1/zstd.1 + zstdcat.1/unzstd.1/zstdless.1 symlinks
No ldconfig call in either install rule, so SandboxInstall is not disturbed.
